prompt-stack/v32/02_overlays/PROMPT_search_reasoning_overlay.md:157:### 3.10 Search Stop Condition
prompt-stack/v32/02_overlays/PROMPT_search_reasoning_overlay.md:158:Search stop condition is the threshold at which more exploration is no longer justified relative to its expected gain.
prompt-stack/v32/02_overlays/PROMPT_search_reasoning_overlay.md:161:Discovery is the deliberate search for new information, new options, or previously unconsidered possibilities, including unknown unknowns.
prompt-stack/v32/02_overlays/PROMPT_search_reasoning_overlay.md:163:### 3.12 Search Budget
prompt-stack/v32/02_overlays/PROMPT_search_reasoning_overlay.md:164:Search budget is the bounded allowance for branching, comparison, iteration, latency, and token expenditure used for search and reasoning.
prompt-stack/v32/02_overlays/PROMPT_search_reasoning_overlay.md:167:Technique fit is the degree to which a reasoning technique matches the actual decision need, risk level, ambiguity level, and budget.
