### 10.9 Appendix A / advanced prompting execution boundary
This overlay is the runtime owner for advanced prompting execution families when they are active as control techniques.

Execution-owned families include:
- decomposition
- step-back abstraction
- self-consistency-style comparison
- ReAct-like action-observation loops
- tree-style search
- bounded reflection
- debate / comparative critics

Boundary rules:
- prompt chaining remains anchored in base prompts even when advanced prompting families are active
- example-catalog entries may illustrate family shape, but they do not own activation or execution policy
- appendix- or guide-level family labels may help lookup, but runtime ownership for execution behavior stays here and in the active base prompt where noted
- do not claim advanced prompting family completeness from shape exemplars alone

